                description: r#"The consumer is multiple simulation planes, then 3D. An inventory found 60 sites in 23 Rust files that build or drop the third axis by hand (51 not routed through a named seam), 1 shader line, 78 gizmo calls that draw in world XY, and the 2D engine. There is no WorldScale type since the P2 flip, so a frame cannot compose there; the seam on the path is the 2D-to-3D lift (PosRot). Detail: docs/frames-decision.md."#,
                decision: true,
                options: [
                    (
                        label: "(a) Frame value type",
                        caption: r#"A PlaneFrame value type (ported from PR #208) in gradiance-core at the 2D-to-3D lift, one instance (world XY); route every site through it and add a CI ratchet. Authored and saved state stays plane-local 2D. Cost: small, no format change. Gives no datums or named planes yet."#,
                    ),
                    (
                        label: "(b) Authored datums",
                        caption: r#"Frames and simulation planes become authored entities that bodies reference by StableId, with commands, records, undo, inspector and verbs. Unlocks named and moving planes and CAD sketch planes. Cost: large, a format bump, and it still needs (a)'s lift; nothing consumes it yet."#,
                    ),
                    (
                        label: "(c) Defer to the 3D engine",
                        caption: r#"Decide frames with the engine choice (PR #208's question). Cost: nothing now, but unrouted sites keep growing, and the engine choice itself needs the plane seam first."#,
                    ),
                ],
            ),
